every fast and furious film has provoked  squabbles among fans and those squabbles  have only gotten bigger  as the franchise has grown from casting  decisions to plot twists  these are the times a fast and furious  franchise outraged fans the most  every fast and furious movie is a micro  time capsule  of what was hot in popular culture at  the time of its filming  the original film was in the dead center  of a time when light washed jeans  hollister shirts  and massive aftermarket spoilers were a  significant part of the culture  the early films were so beholden to  trends that they made an entire movie  without the original cast  just to cash in on the surging  popularity of a japanese racing style  the casting of dwayne the rock johnson  was an unquestionably smart decision  but will also serve as a glimpse of a  time when the wrestler turned actor was  coming into the peak of his box office  powers  i thought so other casting decisions  didn't receive the same sort of love as  johnson's  fans absolutely lost it when they  realized that rapper iggy azalea  played a small part in furious 7 and  they took to the internet to vent about  it though the part was inconsequential  and the film was still a hit  some people admitted it made them  properly angry  glasgow is a working class city full of  the exact kind of folks that would  delight in the fast gangs constant  heists  from greedy companies however being a  worker means having to get up in the  morning  and the shooting of fast and furious 6  made that more than a little difficult  according to reports from the daily  record locals were furious about two  weeks of nighttime filming  that included loud car based stunts  explosions and gunfire  it took hombraj at the fact that they  had not been warned of the night shoot  until right before they began  and complained repeatedly glasgow's film  office painted a different picture  saying that the film crew behind the  movie had given residents ample warning  at least the stunts looked good on the  big screen while most franchise fans  would be ecstatic at the idea of a new  film  a number of people in the fast fanbase  thought it was crass when the franchise  opted to continue  after the death of a core cast member  given the focus on family  quite a few fans were angry when fate of  the furious was announced as the eighth  film in the series  continuing the series without paul  walker didn't sit right with people who  had followed the franchise from  small-scale drag racing caper  to international gang of car driving  superheroes  some fans claim they would never see the  film while others simply worried on  social media that carrying gun after  walker's emotional send-off  would cheapen the ending of furious  seven still fate was a hit and the ninth  film was announced after its release  fate of the furious gave fans more  reason to be angry than paul walker's  absence  the plus of the eighth installment in  the series pitted dominic tiretto  against his surrogate family which the  trailers made clear  since the movies or stress the  importance of created families and  friendly bonds  antareto has put his life on the line  countless times to save his crew  dom turning his back on that and even  threatening to kill his friends  sparked anger when the trailer was  released fans wondered aloud why the  franchise would take such a turn  particularly in the wake of the loss of  paul walker in the real world  and the loss of friendly characters like  han within the fast universe  for certain viewers it felt like the end  of a beloved story  you lost the minute you interrupted my  honeymoon  of course it was later revealed that  dom's turn in fate was only part of a  blackmail scheme  by the end of the film he'd returned to  his family defeated the bad guys  and even made time for a cookout with  all his friends  han didn't need to be avenged but fans  couldn't have known that  since furious 7 we've been operating  under the assumption that the fan  favorite character  died at the hands of deckard shaw the  mercenary who arrived in that film to  avenge his brother's own defeat  in fast and furious 6. shaw's quest for  vengeance began with han whose seemingly  fatal crash all the way back in tokyo  drift was revealed to be the same crash  that launched deckard's fight  against the toretto crew in a  cliffhanger scene from fast and furious  6.  then came fate of the furious and the  revelation that deckard shaw was not  only walking free after han's death  but actually becoming part of the  toretto gang he even landed his own  spin-off alongside dwayne johnson's  character luke hobbs  who may not have been the most important  member of the toretto crew  but his death was still supposed to mean  something and letting shaw just get away  with it  inspired what's become known as the  justice for han movement among fans  something that will now be addressed in  f9 with the fast universe continuing to  expand  some of the sniping over the films is  coming from inside the franchise  following fate of the furious series  star tyrese gibson  tore into the production of hobbs and  shore the first movie outside of the  franchise's main timeline  saying that the film was not worth  splitting from the official series  in a now deleted instagram post after  the spin-off was released  gibson tore into the film's box office  numbers and this attempt at quote  breaking up the family he also offered  the opportunity for hubs and short stars  dwayne johnson  and jason statham to return for fast  turn to give quote  true fans what they wanted gibson's  comments only serve to stoke reports of  onset feuding between himself  johnson statham and vin diesel at the  moment  everyone seems to be happy with the  direction of their careers  but who knows what the future might hold  as the main furious series  reaches its end check out one of our  newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite movie franchises are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you
 

